{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01Mhetj9on8HAz6w1FxK1mtx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both gates pass (352/352; immutability OK, 48 Red files unchanged). Self-review against the anti-shim requirements: bounding and brief-stripping legs exercise adapter operations (not bare renderers), all seven prompts have golden coverage, provenance comes only from assignment config, empty text cannot land ready, and `inference/` still imports only `shared/` (boundaries check green). One spec tension was resolved deliberately and is recorded below: DD-3 says the failure reason is \"the kind string itself,\" but the Epic 02 queue copies the provider reason verbatim onto exhausted forms and existing immutable tests pin that — so retryable reasons lead with `provider_failure:` (the established Epic 02 reason code) followed by the kind, which is the only format satisfying TC-2.3's \"reason `provider_failure`, last error naming `empty_output`\" without touching queue machinery or Epic 02 tests.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Implemented the Story 3 adapter pipeline behind the unchanged Epic 02 seam: each operation now bounds input where DD-7 applies (summarizeToolResult head+tail+marker under maxInputChars), renders its kind's prompt, calls the host ModelCall, rejects empty/whitespace-only success text as retryable empty_output, and returns trimmed text with config-stamped provenance. Ported the POC's settled smoothing prompt verbatim into smoothing-v1 (the other six templates remain marked pre-dial-in with golden coverage). Handlers copy result.provenance into DerivedFormMetadata at all five form-write sites (messages landForm; turns rendering/projection/chunk-summary); the deterministic provider sets none, so its forms carry none. Wrote prompt goldens for all seven templates plus the two story suites covering TC-2.1, TC-2.2, and TC-2.3, demonstrated red on the new behaviors before implementing, and recorded the new Red files in the immutability manifest.\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts\", \"reason\": \"Five-step operation pipeline: tool-result input bounding (DD-7), empty/whitespace-only success classified empty_output retryable (AC-2.4), output shaping via trim, classified failure reasons (retryable reasons lead with the provider_failure code, kind named next), provenance stamped from assignment config (AC-2.5)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/smoothing-v1.ts\", \"reason\": \"Replaced the pre-dial-in placeholder with the POC's settled smoothing system prompt, ported verbatim (AC-2.3)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\", \"reason\": \"landForm takes ProviderResult and copies result.provenance into form metadata alongside the existing mechanical stamps (DD-4, AC-2.5)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\", \"reason\": \"One-line provenance copy on each of the three turn-owned form writes: turn_rendering (merged with receipts metadata), lower_band_projection, and chunk summaries (DD-4, AC-2.5)\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/inference-adapter.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-2.1 and TC-2.3: seven kinds ready with canned content and assignment provenance, record-authored outcomes/receipts disagreeing with adversarial canned text, handler equivalence under the deterministic provider with no provenance, empty-output retry/exhaustion/shaping legs\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/inference-prompts.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-2.2: per-template goldens with fixture embedding and single-turn shape, registry completeness, brief receipt-stripping proven through the adapter against a detailed-lane contrast, tool-result bounding through the adapter operation\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/goldens/prompts/smoothing-v1.golden.json\", \"reason\": \"Golden pinning the POC-settled smoothing rendering\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/goldens/prompts/tool-call-v1.golden.json\", \"reason\": \"Golden pinning tool-call-v1 rendering\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/goldens/prompts/tool-result-v1.golden.json\", \"reason\": \"Golden pinning tool-result-v1 rendering\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/goldens/prompts/turn-compose-v1.golden.json\", \"reason\": \"Golden pinning turn-compose-v1 rendering\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/goldens/prompts/lower-band-v1.golden.json\", \"reason\": \"Golden pinning lower-band-v1 rendering\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/goldens/prompts/chunk-detailed-v1.golden.json\", \"reason\": \"Golden pinning chunk-detailed-v1 rendering including the receipts section\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/goldens/prompts/chunk-brief-v1.golden.json\", \"reason\": \"Golden pinning chunk-brief-v1 rendering including the outcomes-only section\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Recorded the story's Red-phase test files and goldens for the immutability guard\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"test/inference-adapter.test.ts (6 tests: seven-kinds ready with canned content + provenance; record-authored outcomes/receipts vs adversarial text; handler equivalence with marker content and no provenance; empty_output retry lands ready; all-whitespace exhaustion fails with provider_failure/empty_output; whitespace shaping)\",\n      \"test/inference-prompts.test.ts (19 tests: 7 golden matches, 7 fixture-embedding/single-turn legs, 2 registry-completeness legs, 1 brief receipt-stripping leg through the adapter, 2 tool-result bounding legs)\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 352,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 25\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"cd packages/lhc && pnpm exec vitest run test/inference-adapter.test.ts test/inference-prompts.test.ts (pre-implementation Red check: 6 failed on exactly the new Story 3 behaviors)\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"node scripts/check-test-immutability.mjs (48 Red-phase files unchanged)\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"Degenerate-config corner: a maxInputChars smaller than the truncation marker itself (~80 chars) yields marker-only bounded content slightly over the bound; config validation only requires a positive number. Harmless at the 200_000 default and the test's 200, but dial-in could add a sane floor.\",\n      \"The POC smoothing prompt's protected-literals sentence was ported verbatim even though LHC's smoothing input carries no literals list — the clause is inert by design (post-epic-4-work.md retired the regex-extract-then-verify pattern); noted in the module comment so dial-in can reword under a new versioned name.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"specDeviations\": [\n    \"Retryable failure reasons are formatted `provider_failure: <kind>: <message>` rather than DD-3's literal 'reason is the kind string itself'. The Epic 02 queue copies the provider's reason verbatim onto exhausted forms (failTerminal sets form.reason and metadata.lastError from one string), and immutable Epic 02 tests pin that verbatim copy — so TC-2.3's required exhaustion shape ('reason provider_failure and last error naming empty_output') is only reachable if the adapter authors retryable reasons with the provider_failure code leading, matching the reason-code-before-first-colon convention Epic 02 established. Terminal kinds (auth, invalid_request) stay kind-led and land failed immediately, per the tech design's Error Contract. Story 4's classification tests (TC-3.1 asserts the same exhaustion shape for network) should consume this format.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Run story verification for TC-2.1/2.2/2.3, then proceed to Story 4 (classification table, safeCall timeout/exception containment), which should adopt the provider_failure-led retryable reason format recorded in specDeviations.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1160,"cache_read_input_tokens":175417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1160},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d415efd0-0780-463c-9946-d0cae549777f","uuid":"9bca4052-96f6-46b7-b491-5f1c1e43c55e","request_id":"req_011Cbz9xBDpt3C3wy31VtQCk"}
